   "text": "I read the molecule as a cyclic peptide: a disulfide-bridged penicillamine\u2013penicillamine macrocycle with an N-terminal-to-C-terminal arm and a lipidated lysine side arm. I assigned stereochemistry from the wedges and hashes where they are drawn. Where a centre has no clear wedge or hash (Trp, Asn, Thr), I assumed the L configuration.\n\n**Arm out of the ring (C-terminal end first):**\n- Glycinamide carrying an N-methyl group, with its nitrogen acylated by L-3-pyridylalanine.\n- L-Asn, then L-Glu (free acid side chain).\n- 4-Aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid residue.\n- L-2-naphthylalanine, then L-Tyr whose phenol oxygen carries a 2-aminoethyl group.\n- This Tyr is acylated by the carbonyl of the first penicillamine, which opens the ring.\n\n**Macrocycle (going around):**\n- L-Pen (penicillamine, the first one).\n- L-Lys with an acetylated side-chain amine.\n- 7-Methyl-L-Trp, L-Thr and L-Asn.\n- L-Pen (the second one), joined to the first Pen through the S\u2013S bridge between the two C(CH3)2 carbons.\n\n**Lipidated lysine on the second Pen:**\n- A D-Lys whose side-chain amine is acylated by succinic acid. That succinyl group is amidated by a trimethylammonium-bearing 3-aminobutanoic acid unit, which has the R centre shown by its hash.\n- The Lys \u03b1-nitrogen carries two OEG units (\u2013C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013), then a \u03b3-linked L-Glu.\n- The Glu nitrogen carries a C20 diacid acyl group (C(=O)(CH2)18COOH). I estimated the chain length from the drawing's proportions, so the count of 18 CH2 groups is the least certain part.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1cccnc1)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)C1(CCOCC1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H]1NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@H](CC(=O)O)C[N+](C)(C)C)NC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O